SWEET AUDIO DEV (patch 0173, plan A11), on top of 0172 (boot-arg sweetaoc=8 + sweetamp=1). USER DECISION 2026-11-18 ("ignore safety checks for
now. Let's get to something usable in iOS ASAP"). As sweetaoc=7 (HALO load + start, AOC stream, the stock CS35L41 power-up of sweet_amp_pwr.h), but
without the 75 s delay and, in place of the 5.4 s tone window, a service loop (sweet_amp_pwr.h amp_pwr_serve -> sweet_aoc_start.c swau_cb_serve):
/dev/sweetaudio (contract audio/sweetaudio/sweetaudio_dev.h, copied as bsd/dev/sweetaudio_dev.h; doc 54 s.4): root:wheel 0666, one writer (EBUSY),
48 kHz 2 ch S16LE, non-blocking write into an 8192-frame FIFO (sweet_audio_fifo.h), drain from 960 frames and after each underrun, underrun =
silence, close plays out, ioctls INFO / POS / GAIN (software scale in 1 dB steps, clamped to [-96 dB, -10 dB], default -20 dB) / FLUSH. The AOC
feed of 0167 (swau_feed, every 1 ms, only what the AOC consumed) takes its PCM from the FIFO (swau_ring.pull) and pads with silence. Kernel
self-test right after the power-up through the same FIFO: 2 beeps (1 kHz, 0.5 s on / off, -10 dBFS PCM x -20 dB = -30 dBFS as 0172). Amps stay
on (fed silence) until a software reset: sweet_restart.c calls sweet_audio_stop_hook before sweet_machine_reset (timer, remote, reboot(2); not
panic), which stops the loop and waits <= 1 s (counter) for the 0172 stock power-down + DSP stop + AOC close + amp restore. No amp register
access while serving (gpp23 shared with the touch CS, 0166): the 0172 IRQ1_STATUS1 checks of the tone window are left out. Lines "SWEET AUDIO:
a11: ...", "SWEET AUDIO: dev open/close ...". Host test: shim/audio_fifo_host_test.c (FIFO, start threshold, underrun, close play-out, gain).

